From 652c37e93b916e5f2c5a72dc58d2972878d07136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Zampolin <jack.zampolin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:39:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(core): an id one connection holds twice stays in the
 demultiplexing table after its session ends (fails)

sync_cids registers each id of the new list the old list lacks and removes each id of the old list the new list
lacks, one table entry per list entry. When two ids of one connection are the same four bytes and enter in one
sync, the table gets two entries; when they leave one at a time the first departure removes nothing and the second
(or free_slot) removes one, so one entry stays for good, naming the slot. A sub-session's ids derive from the
parent's id secret and the (cc, cs) the dialer sends, so a peer finds a colliding pair offline (2^32 BLAKE3 trials).
The test opens such a sub-session on a real endpoint, drives the victim's window past index 2 and closes it: the
table still maps the id to the freed slot. Adds the trace-feature views trace_demux, trace_cids and trace_session.
